to the settings of the PC  version and what every one of them does  there's an excellent guide written by a  Durante over on PC gamer comm for those  of you who don't know Durante is the guy  who developed this little miracle called  DS fix for Dark Souls 1 PC it turned the  PC port for Dark Souls 1 from a terrible  shameful port into what we deserved he  improved the framerate allowed us to  alter settings improved mouse and  keyboard controls and gave us all the  settings we wanted from a PC game he's  someone from our community who went  above and beyond and he did a great  service for us he did a great service  for from software and also Namco Bandai  making us all forget what a terrible  shame Dark Souls was on PC I mean think  about this from Namco and from his point  of view this guy single-handedly saves  Dark Souls PC from a world of criticism  I think I speak on behalf of everybody  and that's Namco that's from software  and that's all consumers who use dsfix  when I say thank you and hey I've  managed to find his donation page online  where he's probably earned a fraction of  what he deserves  for creating and support  dsfix for years even when darksouls pc  was updated and his mod was made  obsolete he went back numerous times and  fixed it so it would work the link to  this PayPal donation page is on the  second line in the description and if  you have a couple of bucks left over  from buying the pc version i don't i  can't think of anyone better to throw  them to and back to the pc version of  Dark Souls 2 I do think it's worth Abay  especially if you have anything near a  mid-range or if you're enough of a soul  span to warrant getting the definitive  version and most of you on this channel  might just be that it undoubtedly is the  better version while we might never get  the truly next-gen product that was  displayed in TGS demos we received  something that was a damn sight better  than most PC versions and a damn sight  better than what I was worried we would  get this is a company that has really  little experience in the PC space and  hey the game is also available on Steam  so if you don't have enough for a full  price copy right now then just watch  that price drop rapidly in the next few  months and years and pick it up them if  you enjoy my videos feel free to click  here and figure out what kindling the  channel is all about the next video is  going to be a big one most likely so  look forward to that I'll catch you guys  next time later  [Music]  you
 

